<p>Wet tail is the name hamster owners and small-animal vets use for a severe, fast-moving diarrheal illness in hamsters, most often seen in young Syrian (golden) hamsters shortly after they are brought home. It is a true emergency: a hamster that seems fine in the morning can be seriously ill, or worse, within 24 to 48 hours. This guide covers what to look for, what causes it, and exactly what to do if you suspect it.</p>

